TITLE:: LocalClient
summary:: represents a listener to a remote sclang application
categories:: Networking
related:: Classes/Client, Classes/ClientFunc, Overviews/JITLibExtensions

DESCRIPTION::
Note:: Passing a nil address to LocalClient will make it respond to any remote client
and try to match any message that is sent from a client object.
If it is expected to listen to a specific remote client, the address of that client should be used.::

CLASSMETHODS::

private:: default, initClass

METHOD:: named
access all named instances

METHOD:: stop
stop all instances


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: start
start listening to the world

METHOD:: stop
stop listening to the world

METHOD:: reply
reply to a sender with a message

METHOD:: remove
remove from client list

METHOD:: disallow

METHOD:: isListening
return whether localclient is listening to the world

METHOD:: password
set the password for interpreter access from outside

METHOD:: allowInterpret
open the interpreter to the world (potential hacking danger)

METHOD:: disallow
close the interpreter access

private:: minit, replyAddr, defaultAddr, resp, add
